{
  "0": "Learning objective: add 0.1 * mean(softplus(0.5 + negative_score - positive_score)) to the existing loss, using only the negatives already sampled. Explicit positive-negative separation may improve HR@10 without additional sampling. Preserve architecture, scoring, optimizer and training schedule. Apply to all four datasets, with one independently trained model per category.",
  "1": "Training strategy: halve the current learning rate while retaining the existing optimizer, batch size, scheduler, regularization and 200-epoch cap. Smaller updates may reduce the validation oscillation and early degradation seen in the supplied trace, particularly for Electronics. Preserve features, architecture, scoring and loss. Train one model per category across all four datasets with seed 42.",
  "2": "Sequence modeling: halve the current maximum causal context length, rounding up with a minimum of two interactions, and retain the most recent events in chronological order. Apply identical truncation during training and prediction. Shorter histories may reduce stale-interest interference and recurrent computation. Preserve embeddings, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer; retain all four category models and supplied splits.",
  "3": "Interaction mechanism: introduce a jointly trained diagonal compatibility vector initialized to ones: replace the final dot product between interest and candidate vectors with sum_d(w_d * interest_d * candidate_d). This starts at the existing compatibility and can learn which dimensions best distinguish candidates with few additional parameters. Preserve GRU, history readout, features, loss and optimizer. Use one model per category across all four datasets and mirror scoring in the predictor writer."
}
